1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1790
2 PLAC Poland
1 FAMS @F1@
1 NOTE (documented, by name only) Named as father of Izrael in Klimontow death act 40/1867:
2 CONT "syn Rywena i Lacy". No act of his own located. Birth year estimated from his son's age.
2 CONT The surname Rywen-bajrych is built on this given name.
1 NOTE ** MY OWN ERROR, MADE AND CORRECTED 5 Aug 2026 - LEFT VISIBLE. ** I read Klimontow
2 CONT marriage act 4/1834 as making Jeremiasz "urodzonym tu w Klimontowie z RYWENA y Laji" and
2 CONT on that basis upgraded this couple to documented, gave them the trade of bakalarstwo, and
2 CONT entered Jeremiasz as Izrael's brother. Then I read the ALEGAT to the same act - an Akt
2 CONT Znania sworn before the mayor of Klimontow eight days earlier - which states at length
2 CONT and unambiguously that Jeremiasz's father is HERCYK Rywenbayrych, bakalarz. At maximum
2 CONT magnification the register word is NOT securely legible to me either way. A purpose-built
2 CONT identity document outweighs my uncertain reading of a register line, so Jeremiasz is
2 CONT entered under Hercyk the bakalarz (@I54@) and THIS COUPLE REVERTS TO PROBABLE, resting
2 CONT on the 1867 act alone as before.
1 SOUR @S1@

