2 NOTE Birth act 37/1881, Wojslawice (a37_81_top.jpg, a37_81_bot.jpg; unit 45, scan 24,
3 CONT left page). Registered 15/27 November 1881. The child was born in the VILLAGE OF
3 CONT KRASNICZYN on 8/20 November 1881. Declarant: MOSZKO MOSKAL, SHOEMAKER, aged 35, an
3 CONT inhabitant of the village of Krasniczyn. Mother: RUCHLA LAJA nee BIRMAN, aged 26.
3 CONT Witnesses: Kiwa Becher, worker, 41, and Gersz Gruman, worker, 40. Name given in
3 CONT the act as GENIYA, latinised in the margin as "Henia".
2 NOTE The JRI-Poland index row read "Chania 1881"; reading the act itself settled it as
3 CONT GENIYA / Henia (finding 115).
1 NOTE ENTERED 22 Aug 2026, together with her sister Brana-Gitla @I1154@. Same omission:
2 CONT the act was read on 20 Aug 2026 and never entered.
2 CONT IDENTIFICATION: as for Brana-Gitla, the mother Ruchla-Laja nee Birman @I1066@
2 CONT fixes the father as ABRAM-Moszko @I1062@.
2 CONT AGE CONTROL (finding 115): the mother's stated age runs 19 (Jan 1875) - 26 (Nov
2 CONT 1881) - 27 (Nov 1882), a perfect sequence giving b. ~1855. The witness Kiwa Becher
2 CONT is 35 in 1875 and 41 in 1881 - exactly six years. Same household, same village.
