1 NOTE >>> RESOLVED 29 August 2026, AND THIS RECORD IS NOW A DUPLICATE OF @I6@. <<<
2 CONT The old note read: "UNRESOLVED. Klimontow birth act 19/1852 names Hercyk Rywenbayrych,
2 CONT trader, aged 40, of house no. 122, and his wife RYFKA, aged 35 - not Ruchla. Either
2 CONT there were two contemporaries both called Hercyk, or the clerk wrote the wrong given
2 CONT name. Entered separately rather than merged, so the problem stays visible."
2 CONT IT WAS THE CLERK. Klimontow DEATH ACT 14/1850, read from the image on 29 Aug 2026,
2 CONT names the parents of the dead infant Majer as "CHERCYKA i RUCHLI z LEWKOW
2 CONT RYWENBAJRYCHOW, handlarzy w Klimontowie" - Hercyk and RUCHLA "z Lewkow", the very
2 CONT formula the 1852 clerk attached to a "Ryfka". The maiden name is the same in 1850,
2 CONT 1852 and 1854; only the given name slipped, in 1852 alone.
2 CONT His stated ages agree as well: 33 (1845), 37 (1847), 40 (1852), 42 (1854).
2 CONT >>> This @I17@ and his wife @I18@ are the SAME PEOPLE as @I6@ and @I8@. Their child
2 CONT Szaydla @I19@ has been moved to @F4@. The two shell records are kept, empty of family
2 CONT links, so that the mistake and its correction stay legible; they are not ancestors and
2 CONT should not be counted as people.
1 NOTE SHARPENED 29 Aug 2026, from the images of all three acts. It is not only the wife's
2 CONT GIVEN name that disagrees - her MAIDEN name disagrees too, and differently each time:
2 CONT   act 12/1847 - Ruchla "z Sternebugow", he is an OIL TRADER (handlarz oleju), 37,
3 CONT house no. 309
2 CONT   act 19/1852 - Ryfka  "z Lewkow",      he is a trader, 40, house no. 122
2 CONT   act 27/1854 - Ruchla "z Lemkowiczow", he is a trader, 42, house no. 605
2 CONT THE AGES FIT ONE MAN (born about 1810-1812). THE WIVES DO NOT FIT ONE WOMAN. Three
2 CONT different maiden names in seven years cannot be explained by a slip of the given
2 CONT name alone, which was the working theory until now.
2 CONT >>> The remaining readings: two remarriages inside seven years; or two distinct men
3 CONT of the same name and near-identical age in one small town; or a clerk who copied
3 CONT maiden names carelessly. Nothing in these three acts decides between them.
2 CONT >>> WHAT WOULD DECIDE IT: the Klimontow DEATH register 1847-1854, for a Ruchla or a
3 CONT Ryfka Rywenbajrych. Two burials would prove the remarriages; none would point to two
3 CONT men. Not yet searched.
1 SOUR @S15@

