1 NOTE >>> RESOLVED 29 August 2026. THIS IS RUCHLA @I8@, AND THIS RECORD IS A DUPLICATE. <<<
2 CONT The reading itself was verified first, from the image at high magnification: birth act
2 CONT 19/1852 does say "z Malzonki iego RYFKI z LEWKOW lat trzydziesci piec liczacy". The
2 CONT word is short, ends in -kow, and has no -icz- in it.
2 CONT WHAT SETTLED IT was a different act. Klimontow DEATH ACT 14/1850 (@S1056@) names the
2 CONT parents of the infant Majer as "CHERCYKA i RUCHLI Z LEWKOW RYWENBAJRYCHOW" - the same
2 CONT maiden formula, on RUCHLA. So "Ryfka" in 1852 is the clerk's slip on the GIVEN name,
2 CONT and the maiden name is the constant that runs through 1850, 1852, 1854, 1863 and 1867.
2 CONT Her stated age fits too: 35 in 1852 gives about 1817, and Ruchla's own 1847 statement
2 CONT of 30 gives the same year.
1 NOTE ON THE MAIDEN NAME ITSELF - "z Lewkow" is a PATRONYMIC, daughter of LEWEK, not a
2 CONT surname. Two grounds. (1) Lewek is a given name, the Yiddish Lejwe/Lejb; the Checiny
2 CONT kahal certificate of 1824 (@S1053@) writes the identical formula out in full for
2 CONT another woman as "ESTER LEWKOWNA", Ester daughter of Lewek - see @I1179@. (2) The
2 CONT Klimontow clerk uses "z ...ow" for both surnames and patronymics, so the construction
2 CONT settles nothing by itself; what settles it is the word inside. On the very page facing
2 CONT this act he writes "z KIMLOW" (act 18/1852), and elsewhere "z MELECHOW" (26/1854) -
2 CONT Kimel and Melech being given names, exactly like Lewek - alongside true surnames like
2 CONT "z Grynbergow".
2 CONT >>> NOT to be connected to LEWEK @I1186@ of Checiny: different town, different
2 CONT generation, a very common name. No evidence joins them and none is claimed.
1 NOTE >>> AND THIS UNLOCKS @I8@. Ruchla's maiden formula had been read nine different ways
2 CONT and left open: "z Leml(ow)" 1845, "z Lemkowiczow" 1854, "z Kimetow" 1856,
2 CONT "z Komkowiczow" 1861, "z Lemkowiczow" 1863 and 1867, "z Lemelow" 1865. Re-read at high
2 CONT magnification on 29 Aug 2026, the 1854 word is LEWKOWICZOW - the third letter is a
2 CONT single-humped w, not an m. LEWKOWICZ and LEWKOW are the same patronymic in its long
2 CONT and short forms. See @I8@.
1 SOUR @S15@
1 SOUR @S1056@
