2 NOTE >>> READ IN THE ORIGINAL 21 Aug 2026 at full magnification. Opatow residents'
3 CONT index (skorowidz), APK 24/6/0/-/13 = unit 24686192, scan 54, page 133, row 359.
3 CONT Her row carries a remark in the UWAGI column, in a later hand:
3 CONT ** "14/V 1935 r. Warszawa, ul. Walicow 13-1." **
3 CONT ⇒ SHE LEFT OPATOW FOR WARSAW ON 14 MAY 1935, aged seventeen, to a named
3 CONT address: WALICOW STREET 13, APARTMENT 1.
3 CONT >>> ON THE GHETTO BOUNDARY - AND THE BOUNDARY, NOT THE INTERIOR. Checked
3 CONT 21 Aug 2026 against the street's documented history; an earlier note here said
3 CONT flatly that Walicow "fell inside the ghetto" - that was too strong, and is
3 CONT withdrawn. What the sources support:
3 CONT (1) On 16 Nov 1940 MOST of Walicow was enclosed, but the wall CROSSED the street
3 CONT     in two places - about 100 m from the Chlodna end, and about 50 m of the
3 CONT     WESTERN side from the Ceglana corner.
3 CONT (2) The wall of the Jung brewery at WALICOW 11 - the house NEXT DOOR, and on
3 CONT     the same odd-numbered side as no. 13 - WAS the ghetto boundary from
3 CONT     November 1940 to August 1942. It survives, with a plaque reading
3 CONT     "In this place in the years 1940-1942 Walicow street was DIVIDED by the
3 CONT     ghetto wall."
3 CONT (3) The division CHANGED: in December 1941 the EASTERN side between Chlodna and
3 CONT     Krochmalna was taken OUT of the ghetto and the western side up to Chlodna
3 CONT     put IN; in August 1942 the area south of Chlodna went to the "Aryan" side
3 CONT     except the Toebbens workshop.
3 CONT ⇒ WHETHER NO. 13 STOOD INSIDE OR OUTSIDE CANNOT BE STATED - it depends on the
3 CONT   side of the street and on the date, and the sources do not settle no. 13.
3 CONT ⚠ AND THE PRIOR QUESTION: she is recorded here in MAY 1935, five and a half
3 CONT   years BEFORE the ghetto existed. Nothing in this document says she was still
3 CONT   at this address in 1940.
2 NOTE ★ CORROBORATED BY FAMILY TESTIMONY, 21 Aug 2026. Amotz asked his father, who
3 CONT knew nothing of any Warsaw address - but said, independently: ** "before the war
3 CONT she moved to Warsaw to study SEWING." **
3 CONT ⇒ TWO INDEPENDENT SOURCES AGREE ON THE MOVE: the Opatow register fixes it to
3 CONT 14 May 1935 with a street and apartment; the family remembers the reason.
3 CONT The father did NOT supply the address, so this is not circular - the testimony
3 CONT was given without knowledge of the document.
3 CONT >>> AND IT FITS HER AGE: a girl of seventeen and a half leaving a small town
3 CONT alone is explained by an apprenticeship, not by a family move - her parents and
3 CONT sister stayed registered at Opatow.
3 CONT ○ CONTEXT, NOT EVIDENCE: the Walicow-Ceglana-Prosta quarter was Warsaw's
3 CONT garment district. Do not read more into that than context.
2 NOTE ★ THE ADDRESS ITSELF VERIFIED, 21 Aug 2026 - the house existed and was occupied.
3 CONT Warsaw address book, "Ksiega adresowo-gospodarcza miasta stolecznego Warszawy,
3 CONT Cz. III e: Spis wlascicieli domow" (1939 edition; its figures are stated as of
3 CONT 31 December 1938), page 161, column 3, under the heading WALICOW:
3 CONT ** "13, VII - Stradecki Antoni (1109)." **
3 CONT ⇒ WALICOW 13 WAS A STANDING RESIDENTIAL HOUSE, owner ANTONI STRADECKI,
3 CONT mortgage number 1109, in the SEVENTH police district (komisariat VII).
3 CONT >>> AND THE NEIGHBOURS CONFIRM THE QUARTER: no. 3 Silberberg Judka, no. 10 Kac
3 CONT i Sitkowski, no. 12 Aszkenejzer Hersz and Gruenberg Gitla, no. 6 Br. Szpilfogiel
3 CONT - a Jewish street, as expected.
3 CONT ⚠ WHAT THIS DOES NOT SHOW: the book lists OWNERS ONLY, never tenants. A girl of
3 CONT seventeen in rented rooms could not appear in it. And the owner's name is POLISH,
3 CONT so she was a lodger or a tenant - she did NOT move in with a relative who owned
3 CONT the house.
3 CONT ⚠ AND THE DATE GAP: this edition is 1939, four years after May 1935. Ownership
3 CONT could have changed in between.
3 CONT ★ THE PRACTICAL GAIN: KOMISARIAT VII. The Warsaw Jewish vital registers are filed
3 CONT BY POLICE DISTRICT (see metryki.genealodzy.pl id683). If she married or was
3 CONT registered in Warsaw, the seventh district is where to look.
3 CONT >>> Source images: albert/sources/warszawa/walicow/
3 CONT >>> This remark was NOT noticed in the earlier readings of this scan; the roman
3 CONT numeral and page number were read, the UWAGI column was not.
1 SOUR @S91@
1 SOUR @S92@

