1 NAME Fajga Rachla /Rywenbajrych/
2 GIVN Fajga Rachla
2 SURN Rywenbajrych
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1920
2 PLAC Opatow, Poland
1 DEAT
2 PLAC Skarzysko-Kamienna camp, Poland
2 NOTE Shot. Chana's younger sister - it was Amotz's memory of this murdered sister that
3 CONT opened the whole Opatow line.
3 CONT CONFLICT, RESOLVED IN THE FAMILY'S FAVOUR: the 1988 Opatow memorial list places her
3 CONT at Treblinka on 23 October 1942 with her parents. But a contemporaneous German camp
3 CONT document - the lists of Skarzysko-Kamienna inmates designated "sick", November 1942
3 CONT to February 1943 - carries a FAJGA RYWENBAJRYCH, i.e. alive and in the camp AFTER
3 CONT that date. A record made at the time outweighs a list compiled by survivors in 1988,
3 CONT whose compilers evidently assumed the whole household died in the October deportation.
3 CONT At Skarzysko the "sick" designation was in practice a selection list.
3 CONT The family's account was right.
1 FAMC @F11@
1 NOTE (documented) A fifth Page of Testimony for her surfaced 14 Aug 2026: item 394902,
2 CONT filled in by her great-uncle MOSHE Wajsblum on 26 June 1957 as sheet 13146-1 - the
2 CONT FIRST sheet of the same envelope as his Pages for Bejla, Reizel and the two husbands.
2 CONT He wrote her as "Feiga BEIRACH", his usual shorthand for Rywenbajrych, father Tuvia,
2 CONT mother Bila, born Opatow, single; field 11 reads only "extermination" (hashmada) -
2 CONT no place, no date - and fields for birth year and children are blank. The only Page
2 CONT for her by someone of her parents' generation. It adds no date and does not disturb
2 CONT the Skarzysko resolution above.
