1 NOTE (documented) Son of Moszek and Gella: he said so himself. The 1966 Opatow necrology
2 CONT entries for "Moshe Veisblum" and "Gele Veisblum nee Ginzburg" (Yad Vashem 12567734,
2 CONT 12567735) each carry "informant: Alter Veisblum, Son". He supplied his parents'
2 CONT entries to the memorial book and filed no Pages of Testimony at all - the submitter
2 CONT index holds exactly those two records for him, in every spelling (findings/056-057).
2 CONT The necrology entry also confirms, from a second source, that Gella's father was
2 CONT Khanina - the JRI finding of 050 par. 5.
2 CONT ** 15 Aug 2026: his gravestone says it a second time and independently - "Alter
2 CONT Chaim son of Moshe Natan [Nossen]". A third kind of source (a stone, cut by his
2 CONT own family) after the necrology, where he was himself the informant, and the JRI
2 CONT index. It also gives Moszek a fuller name; see @I20@. findings/088. **
1 NOTE (probable) His war: Starachowice-Wierzbnik camp, then Buchenwald, then Theresienstadt,
2 CONT where he was liberated - per the Memorial Book record above, same identification
2 CONT caveat. First survivor of this branch with an exact birth date.
2 CONT ** CORRECTED 15 Aug 2026: he was NOT in Israel. Canadian voters lists place him in
2 CONT York, Ontario in 1965 and in 1968. The 1966 memorial book was published in Tel
2 CONT Aviv, but its informant wrote from Toronto. The identification of the Theresienstadt
2 CONT survivor with this Alter never rested on the city, so it is unaffected. **
1 NOTE (documented) After liberation, recovered 15 Aug 2026 (findings/088). By 1947 he was
2 CONT living in KREIS SCHWABMUENCHEN, Bavaria, registered on an Arolsen F18 list of
2 CONT "55 Jews who were living in Kreis Schwabmuenchen in 1947" (ref 8806110) - entry 50,
2 CONT "Weisblum Alter, 24.10.03, Opatow, last residence Starachowice", with his wife Hela
2 CONT immediately below him at entry 51. ** Entries 52 and 53 on that same page are Hena
2 CONT and Chaja Weisblum of Opatow, the daughters of Chil and Sura (findings/087) - four
2 CONT Wajsblums from Opatow among 55 people in one Bavarian district. Suggestive of kin
2 CONT who regrouped; it is a residence list, not a family list, and proves no relation. **
2 CONT He left Bremen on 25 Jun 1948 from the Bremen-Grohn resettlement camp, by air
2 CONT ("Flug Nr. 3"), aged 44, married, occupation millworker, arriving Prestwich (a
2 CONT Jewish suburb of Manchester), England. He was in York, Ontario by 1965, and died
2 CONT in Toronto in 1998.
1 NOTE (documented) Married twice. Hela Baranek (@I77@, @F67@) died in Toronto on
2 CONT 13 Mar 1974; the following year, on a 1975 Brooklyn marriage licence (index number
2 CONT 10310), "Alter Weisbloom" married RACLA GRYNBAL. She is not entered as a person in
2 CONT this file - the licence index gives nothing but the two names and the year, and no
2 CONT record has yet been found placing her in Toronto with him.
1 NOTE (documented) An Arolsen tracing-file index row of 1947 carries "Alter Weisblum,
2 CONT b. 24 Oct 1905" - case 381471 (findings/065). The birth date matches the
2 CONT Theresienstadt Memorial Book to the day, from an independent record group; someone
2 CONT was traced by him, or he was traced, in 1947. The file itself has not been obtained.
