1 NOTE (documented) The family stands on three legs, each independent of the others:
2 CONT (1) the 1921 Opatow town register, read in findings/022, which put Bejla under
2 CONT Rafael and Fajga; (2) Moshe's five Pages of one day in 1957 - he calls Bejla and
2 CONT Reizel "Brother" and their husbands "Brother-in-law", making him their sibling and
2 CONT the parents his own; (3) Shlomo's independent 1955 Pages naming Szoszana's parents
2 CONT Rafael and Tzipora. Discovered in this order: 022 first raised Rafael; 053-054
2 CONT read Moshe's forms; 056-058 exhausted Yad Vashem, merged Reizel with Szoszana and
2 CONT closed the sibling list. NO OTHER CHILDREN are attested anywhere searched; the
2 CONT list is closed to current knowledge, not proven complete. Marriage: nothing found;
2 CONT Opatow marriage scans for the plausible years sit in the GenBaza gap (1845-1877)
2 CONT or behind its account wall.
1 NOTE ** THE OUTSTANDING TEST: Opatow birth act 8/1892, first item in the Sandomierz
2 CONT letter. If its parents read Rafael and Fajga, this family gains its first
2 CONT contemporaneous civil record; if not, Bejla's birth act is unfound and the year
2 CONT 1891/92 rests on the memorial list and the Pages alone. **

