2 NOTE RE-CORRECTED 15 AUG 2026: the 1894 act itself reads БУТКОВСКАЯ (Butkowska) — the
3 CONT letter long misread as ж is т, confirmed at x8 magnification; the Piatek 1883 register
3 CONT spells the name in Latin script "(Butkowski)", and the whole chain of spellings
3 CONT (Bukowska 1909, "Gutkowska" 1945, Budkowska 2015) settles without remainder. Birth
3 CONT found: Piatek act 22/1872 (JRI index). See albert/findings/032-piatek-buzowski.md.
3 CONT Earlier notes kept below for the audit trail.
2 CONT SURNAME CORRECTED. FOUR renderings now: BUZOWSKA (1894 marriage act), BUKOWSKA (1909
3 CONT death act), "Gutkowska" (CKZP 1945) and **BUDKOWSKA** (the family's 2015 Polish
3 CONT citizenship application). Three of the four open with B, which leaves "Gutkowska" as the
3 CONT lone outlier and further weakens it. The two contemporaneous archival forms still carry
3 CONT the most weight. Original note follows.
2 CONT Three renderings survive: BUZOWSKA / БУЖОВСКАЯ in the 1894 marriage
3 CONT act; BUKOWSKA / БУКОВСКАЯ in the 1909 death act of her son; and "Gutkowska" on the
3 CONT 1945 CKZP slip. In Cyrillic the first two differ by one letter. The 1945 form is the
3 CONT latest and the furthest from the event - written in post-war Warsaw, probably from
3 CONT Chaim's own mouth, decades after his mother's death and with no document to hand.
3 CONT Buzowska is adopted: earliest, most formal, and the only one that also records where
3 CONT she came from. Every earlier search failed because I was looking for a surname that
3 CONT never existed.
