2 NOTE Registered as ALPERT in Poland; ALBERT in Israel. Amotz's paternal grandfather.
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 JUL 1907
2 PLAC Warsaw, Poland
2 NOTE ** OVERSTATED, CORRECTED WITHIN THE HOUR — read this whole note. ** I first wrote that the
3 CONT 2015 application "resolves" the date. It does not, and I should not have said so. The date
3 CONT 11.07.1907 already existed on a CKZP registration card in our own hands; the 1913 came from
3 CONT CKZP slip 12344. Both are POST-WAR SELF-DECLARATIONS of the same class. The 2015 filing
3 CONT simply repeats one of the two - so it tells us **which date the family committed to**, and
3 CONT is NOT an independent source for the year. The conflict is therefore NOT resolved by
3 CONT evidence; it is resolved only as a matter of which the family used.
3 CONT ** 1907 is adopted here** because it is the date the family put before a state authority,
3 CONT and because it is a specific day-month-year rather than a bare year - but it stays ONE
3 CONT post-war declaration against another.
2 NOTE The family's
3 CONT own official Polish citizenship application of 2015 (12-page WNIOSEK to the Wojewoda
3 CONT Mazowiecki) gives him, in a structured field, as born **11 / 07 / 1907**.
3 CONT The competing "1913" came from CKZP slip 12344 ("ur. 1913 W-wa"); a second CKZP card had
3 CONT already given 11.07.1907 and I had left the conflict open. The 2015 filing settles it in
3 CONT favour of 1907 - a date the family committed to in a state document.
3 CONT ** CONSEQUENCE: my whole Warsaw birth-register search ran on the wrong year. ** I read the
3 CONT 1913 alphabetical index of cyrkul VI (unit 72/200/0/-/110, scans 110-114, sections А and
3 CONT Э) and found no Alpert/Albert/Elbert. That negative stands but is irrelevant - it is for
3 CONT a year that is not his. So I redid it on 1907 - and:
3 CONT ** NO 1907 WARSAW JEWISH BIRTH REGISTER SURVIVES IN FOND 72/200/0 AT ALL. ** For 1907 the
3 CONT fond holds only marriages (cyrkul IV = -/66, 151 scans; cyrkul V = -/98, 152 scans) and two
3 CONT unscanned marriage-annex units (-/251, -/252). There are combined birth/marriage/death
3 CONT units for 1906, 1908 and 1909, but none for 1907.
3 CONT ** And JRI's Warsaw birth index has no Alpert/Albert/Elbert birth with a mother RUDLA, and
3 CONT none named Chaim in 1907. ** Indexed Warsaw Alpert/Albert births run 1871-1905 with nothing
3 CONT after Jakow Josif 1905.
3 CONT ** CONCLUSION: on both candidate years the register is gone. Chaim's Warsaw birth act very
3 CONT probably does not survive. ** What remains: another Warsaw fond or duplicate series
3 CONT (unchecked), and asking Daniela Regev what document 11.07.1907 was taken from.
3 CONT The gravestone says only "born Warsaw", which is consistent with either year.
2 NOTE (documented) 13 Aug 2026 - the SECOND Warsaw fond has now been checked too, and it
3 CONT closes the same door from the other side. On metryki.genealodzy.pl the Warsaw Jewish
3 CONT fond is 0200d (id683), 194 units, 1858-1937 - a different scanned body from the
3 CONT szukajwarchiwach fond 72/200/0 discussed above. Its only apparent birth coverage for
3 CONT our two candidate years is unit 1907a, catalogued "U-1907-1913, Urodzenia", 34 files.
3 CONT ** All 11 of its 1907 and 1913 scans were downloaded and read. They are not Jewish. **
3 CONT Every one of the 20 acts is signed by the "Civil Status Officer of the BAPTIST
3 CONT confession, 7th district", and the father in act 2/1907 is Oskar Truderung, pastor of
3 CONT the Warsaw Baptist congregation. The unit is the Warsaw Baptist birth register
3 CONT 1907-1913, misfiled into the Jewish fond. ** So the apparent "6 scans for 1907" and
3 CONT "5 for 1913" are 0 and 0. ** The last possible hiding place, unit 1905a
3 CONT (UMZ-1905-1910), was checked as well: its years are 1905, 1908 and 1910 - not 1907.
3 CONT Ten further units of fond 0200d were sampled and are genuinely Jewish; 1907a is the
3 CONT only anomaly in 1905-1914. See findings/047. This is a statement about what is
3 CONT scanned and online, NOT proof the volumes are lost.
3 CONT ** The live route is no longer Warsaw. ** See findings/048: AP Czestochowa fond 1
3 CONT (= USHMM RG-15.301), sygn. 13801, "Registration of Jews arriving from other towns to
3 CONT Czestochowa, 1941 and 1942", 143 leaves, whose inventory states the lists record name,
3 CONT DATE OF BIRTH, family members, occupation and town of origin. Chaim came to
3 CONT Czestochowa from Warsaw and was there in 1942, so that book should settle 1913 vs 1907.
3 CONT Drafts ready at letters/REQUEST-ap-czestochowa-13801.md and
3 CONT letters/REQUEST-ushmm-reference-RG-15.301.md. Not yet sent.
