1 TITL Yad Vashem Pages of Testimony filed by Moshe Wajsblum, Tel Aviv, 26 June 1957
1 TEXT Five sheets, approval numbers 13146-1 to 13146-5, one envelope, one day:
2 CONT 394902 Fajga-Rachla ("Feiga Beirach", his great-niece, "Uncle"); 881379 Bejla
2 CONT ("Beila Beirach nee Veisblum", "Brother"); 954251 Reizel ("Reizel Schoehnbak nee
2 CONT Veisblum", "Brother"); 3829036 Tuvia ("Tuwja Beirach", "Brother-in-law");
2 CONT 954729 Yehoshua ("Szyju Schoehnhak", "Brother-in-law").
2 CONT Reizel's sheet is the one that names the parents: father Rafael, mother Feiga.
1 NOTE FIRST-HAND, and the earliest testimony this family has. Written by Bejla's own
2 CONT brother, a survivor, thirty years before the 1988 memorial list and forty-four
2 CONT years before the Pages that Amotz's sister Aya filled in. Where Moshe's sheets and
2 CONT Aya's disagree, Moshe was there. He signs from Jaffa Street 6 apt. 3, Tel Aviv-Yafo.
2 CONT Field 11 on every sheet of his reads only "extermination" - he recorded no place
2 CONT and no date of death on any of the five. Scans and enlargements of the fields in
2 CONT albert/sources/yadvashem/. Method and readings in findings/057-058.

0 @S71@ SOUR
1 TITL Yad Vashem Pages of Testimony filed by Shlomo Wajsblum, Ramat Gan, 22 October 1955
1 TEXT Approval numbers 243917 and 243918, consecutive, filled in together: 1651118
2 CONT Yehoshua Szenaug (his uncle - Shlomo is a son of Yehoshua's brother Yekhiel of
2 CONT Tarnobrzeg) and 485661 Szoszana ("Cousin"). He also filed 8652609 and 8652610 for
2 CONT their two children. Yehoshua's sheet is the fullest document in this group: his
2 CONT parents Tzvi and Bluma, born Tarnobrzeg 1890, grocer, died Treblinka 1942, wife
2 CONT "Szoszana WAJSBLUM" aged 42, and in field 14 both children by name and age -
2 CONT Fejga 9 and Cwi 6, Treblinka 1942.
1 NOTE INDEPENDENT of Moshe's envelope: different informant, different town, two years
2 CONT earlier, and the two men were not related to each other - Shlomo's connection runs
2 CONT through Szoszana's husband. That is what makes his "father: Rafael" a genuine second
2 CONT attestation rather than an echo. He is himself a survivor of a camp and a ghetto,
2 CONT both named in his hand at the foot of the forms (not yet read).

