2 DATE ABT 1826
2 PLAC Wystepy, gmina Samsonow, Poland
2 NOTE Aged 23 at her 1849 marriage, of Wystepy village near Samsonow.
1 FAMC @F65@
1 FAMS @F63@
1 NOTE ** THE "TWO RYWKAS" QUESTION - LARGELY RESOLVED 21 Aug 2026. ** In the birth acts of
2 CONT 1850-1852 the mother is "Ryfka"; from 1855 the registers write "Marya", in 1865
2 CONT "Marya z Wajntraubow", and a Kielce death of 1872 records "Rywka Marjem, wife of
2 CONT Kiwa, daughter of SZMUL and Gitla" - while the 1849 bride is daughter of IZRAEL and
2 CONT Gitla. The CRARG sweep of 21 Aug 2026 settles two of the three strands:
2 CONT (a) ONE WOMAN, NOT TWO. Marriage act 7/1894 Radoszyce names the groom's parents as
3 CONT "KIWA CUKIER" and "MARIEM RYWKA nee WINOGRAD, deceased" - both given names in a
3 CONT single person, in a single record. Consistent with her death in 1872.
2 CONT (b) "z WAJNTRAUBOW" IS THE FAMILY'S ALIAS, not another woman. Birth act 89/1865 of
3 CONT Wystempa records "RACHMIL WINOGRAD VEL WAJNTROP, 33" - the same alias, the same
3 CONT village, the same year as the "Marya z Wajntraubow" entry.
2 CONT (c) STILL OPEN: SZMUL vs IZRAEL as her father. Szmul appears twice (the 1872 death;
3 CONT and marriage act 11/1851, where CEJWA Winogrod of Wystepy is daughter of SZMUL and
3 CONT GITLA - the same mother's name), Izrael once (the 1849 marriage). Two against one
3 CONT leans to Szmul; a double given name "Szmul-Izrael" would reconcile them, and his
3 CONT son was in fact named Izrael Kalman. NOT DECIDED - she is left under @F65@ as the
3 CONT 1849 act states. Deciding documents remain the act images of 46/1865 and 14/1872.
2 CONT Rywa's own death is therefore still NOT entered here. See findings/083 and 119.
1 SOUR @S84@

