2 NOTE ** EXACT DATE, FROM THE KAHAL CERTIFICATE ITSELF (@S1050@), read 28 Aug 2026: **
3 CONT "urodzil tutay w miescie Checinach [...] ten sie urodzil dnia 21. Lutego roku
3 CONT Tysiac Siedm Set Dziewiecdziesiatego Piatego, a tak konczy lat Dwadziescia Osm."
3 CONT The certificate also calls him "ARONA MORDKOWICZA na teraz CUKROWSKIM zwanego" -
3 CONT Aron son of Mordka, NOW CALLED Cukrowski: the surname change caught in the act of
3 CONT happening.
2 CONT From marriage act 1/1824 of Strawczyn: "maiacy podlug Swiadectwa z Kachalu
3 CONT Checinskiego wydanego lat dwadziescia dziewiec NIEDOKONCZONE" - twenty-nine not yet
3 CONT complete on 12 January 1824. So born between 13 Jan 1794 and 12 Jan 1795. The age
3 CONT certificate came from the KAHAL OF CHECINY, which places his birth registration
3 CONT there rather than at Strawczyn.
1 MARR
2 DATE 12 JAN 1824
2 PLAC Strawczyn, Poland
1 OCCU potash maker
2 NOTE "Potaznik" in the 1846 act - potash making was the family trade, carried on by Kiwa.
1 RESI
2 PLAC Ruda Strawczynska, Poland
1 FAMS @F64@
1 FAMS @F1073@
1 FAMC @F1071@
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1846 AND 1858
2 PLAC Radoszyce registry district, Poland
2 NOTE ** BRACKETED, NOT FOUND. ** He is alive and working as a potash maker in his son
3 CONT Mosiek's marriage act 9/1846, and marked DECEASED in his son Chaim Wolf's act
3 CONT 18/1858. Two grandsons born 1859 and 1862 were named Aron. The death act itself,
3 CONT somewhere in the Radoszyce register between those years, is the document that would
3 CONT name HIS parents - the next generation back. It has not been searched for.
1 NOTE (documented, by name) Named as father of the groom in Kiwa's 1849 marriage act and in
2 CONT the marriage rows of five other children - Abram 16/1844, Mortka 17/1844, Mosiek
2 CONT 9/1846, Laja 13/1857, Chaim Wolf 18/1858. See @F64@.
1 NOTE (documented) MARRIAGE ACT 1/1824, STRAWCZYN - read from the image 28 Aug 2026. It
2 CONT names HIS PARENTS: Mortka Cukroski, potasznik, "niegdy" of Ruda, and Esterka z
2 CONT Choynow (@F1071@) - two generations further back. It also shows he was a WIDOWER of
2 CONT Sara z Rutkowskich (@I1180@), so this was his second marriage. He signed the act
2 CONT himself, in Hebrew letters: "Aharon Cukrowski".
2 CONT >>> IDENTIFICATION. The act says CUKROSKI, not Cukier. It is the same man on every
2 CONT other axis: same tiny village Ruda, same trade potasznik, wife Taube whose father
2 CONT is Mosko - matching Tauba's documented maiden surname MOSZKOWICZ - and a father
2 CONT called Mortka, after whom their son Mortka ~1823 is named. In 1824 Jewish surnames
2 CONT were three years old; Cukroski to Cukier is ordinary drift. Strong, not certain.
2 CONT See albert/findings/131.
1 SOUR @S84@
