1 NAME Szmul /Szaufer/
2 GIVN Szmul
2 NICK Shmuelke, Shmuel Schafir
2 SURN Szaufer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1836
2 PLAC Wojslawice, Chelm, Lublin, Poland
2 NOTE FOUR independent statements: 26 in Aug 1859 (=> ~1833), 36 in Jan 1873 (=> ~1837),
3 CONT 41 in Oct 1878 (=> ~1837), 55 in Jan 1890 (=> ~1835). The 1873 and 1878 acts AGREE on
3 CONT ~1837; ~1836 taken as the estimate. Born in Wojslawice per both marriage acts.
1 OCCU Roofer and shingle-maker - "gontarz" (1859), "krovelshchik" (1873, 1878)
1 NOTE HE COULD NOT WRITE: at his son Hersz's birth registration in Oct 1878 the clerk noted
2 CONT "the father declared that he does not know how to write" - the act was signed by the
2 CONT witnesses instead. (He did sign the 1890 registration, in Hebrew letters.)
1 RESI
2 PLAC Wojslawice, Chelm, Lublin, Poland
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1920
2 NOTE Inferred: his grandson Shmuel Schafir b. c.1920/21 was named for him (Ashkenazi custom).
1 SOUR @S1004@
1 FAMC @F1023@
1 FAMS @F1024@
1 SOUR @S1014@
1 SOUR @S1015@
1 NOTE _CONF PROVEN 4 Aug 2026. THE REGISTERS SPELL THE FAMILY **SZAUFER** (Cyrillic SHAUFER) -
2 CONT which is why exact-spelling searches for Szafir never found them. Marriage act 1/1873
2 CONT Wojslawice: SZMUL SZAUFER, widower, roofer, 36, born Wojslawice, son of the late CHAIM
2 CONT and LIBA nee Kielner. His occupation in the record matches the memoir exactly.
2 CONT Earlier assessment kept for the record: PROBABLE for the given name - stated only as the peasants' familiar form, twice,
2 CONT in his son's memoir: "Hey, good brothers, Shmuelke has come!" and "Oh, our Jew, our Shmuelke!"
2 CONT PROVEN for everything else, from the memoir itself.
2 CONT A Belz Hasid. Known as a craftsman as far as Chelm and Lublin; re-roofed the town after its
2 CONT fire; walked the villages mending peasants' roofs, often without payment. Imprisoned rather
2 CONT than send his son to the Russian government school; his son heard him saying Psalms in the cell.
2 CONT Married two sisters: the elder died childless, and on the ruling of the Rebbe of Belz he married
2 CONT the younger, then about fifteen, when he was in his forties. Four sons and four daughters.
2 CONT ROOFING WAS THE FAMILY TRADE - cf. the other Wojslawice Szafir household (roofer/tiler) and
2 CONT "Yosele Schafer the roof-tiler" shot off a roof in 1942.
1 FAMS @F1001@
1 FAMS @F1028@

