3 CONT b. ~1856 - PROVEN by convergence of the 1873 and 1878 acts.
1 NOTE _CONF PROVEN 4 Aug 2026 - NAMED AT LAST. Marriage act 1/1873 Wojslawice: the maiden PESIA
2 CONT SZYFMAN, 17, born in Wojslawice, daughter of the late Berek(?) and Dwojra Itta nee KAC,
2 CONT lawful Szyfman spouses; living with her mother as a labourer. Her mother, present, gave
2 CONT consent. Her full name PESIA-RUCHLA appears on Mendel's 1890 birth registration.
2 CONT THE MEMOIR IS CONFIRMED AND EXTENDED: Shmuel married two sisters - the elder first (1859,
2 CONT act 14; she died childless, hence "widower" in 1873) and then Pesia. The sisters were
2 CONT SZYFMAN. She was 17, not 15; he was 36, a widower - which is why a rabbinic ruling
2 CONT (the Belzer Rebbe) would have been sought.
