1 NOTE Four sons and four daughters, per the memoir (S4). EIGHT children are now on record from
2 CONT the Wojslawice birth index and acts: Estera-Malka 1873 (act 23), Chaim Froim 1876
2 CONT (act 39, @I1080@), Hersz/Gersz 1878 (act 30, @I1003@), JOSEF 1881 (act 3, @I1033@),
2 CONT Dwojra-Laia 1883 (act 11, @I1056@), and the three late registrations of 1890 - Menachem
2 CONT Mendel (@I1004@), SRUL LEJB (act 4, @I1091@) and Dawid (act 5).
2 CONT ⚠ THIS GEDCOM IS BEHIND THE SITE DATA. Estera-Malka and Dawid are carried in
2 CONT site/data/people.moskal.json but have no INDI record here yet. Only Josef and Srul-Lejb
2 CONT were added on 14 Aug 2026, because Yad Vashem Pages gave them adult identities; the
2 CONT other two should follow.
2 CONT ** WHAT 14 AUG 2026 ADDED IS NOT TWO NEW SONS BUT TWO ADULT LIVES. ** Josef and Srul-Lejb
2 CONT were already known from the birth index as names with no trade, no family and no fate.
2 CONT Three Pages of Testimony (@S1025@) naming "father Shmuel, mother Pesia / Peshe" now give
2 CONT them both: Josef the roof-tiler of houses 32-33, married to Yokheved, murdered in
2 CONT Wojslawice - which reverses the earlier ruling that his household was a different Szafir
2 CONT family; and Srul-Lejb, as YISRAEL, a merchant in Chelm, murdered there.
2 CONT ⚠ The memoir's count of four sons is now exceeded (Chaim Froim, Hersz, Mendel, Josef,
2 CONT Srul-Lejb, Dawid = six). The register is the harder evidence; the likeliest explanation
2 CONT is that Mendel, writing decades later, counted the brothers who reached adulthood, and
2 CONT that one or two of the 1876-1890 boys died young. Not resolved - stated.
2 CONT >>> OPEN QUESTION REMAINS: the four daughters. Only Estera-Malka and Dwojra-Laia are
2 CONT identified. The Wojslawice registers (FamilySearch films 767024-5) are where the rest are.
