2 PAGE Record 14577491, Malka Moskal (nee Schafir), Holon Cemetery, Bat Yam
1 NOTE _CONF PROVEN. THE WITNESS OF THIS WHOLE HISTORY. Survived the war in the Soviet Union
2 CONT ("in Russia", in her own words on the 2001 form - this one IS documented, in her hand).
2 CONT UNVERIFIED CANDIDATE: IGRA record IGRA-1949-ImmigApr-20200 reads "Malka Muskal, child of
2 CONT Leib, Immigration 1948-, 1949" in an April 1949 list. The surname matches her own spelling,
2 CONT but the patronymic Leib is her HUSBAND's father, not hers (Menachem Mendel). NOT CONFIRMED.
2 CONT Her date of arrival in Israel remains unestablished.
2 CONT Filed TWELVE Pages of Testimony at Yad Vashem in her own handwriting - five at Petah Tikva
2 CONT on 7 January 1957, seven at Bat Yam on 19 September 2001, forty-four years apart - for her
2 CONT mother, her two fallen brothers, and her husband's mother and four sisters.
2 CONT Everything known about the family members who were murdered comes from those twelve pages.
2 CONT HER GRAVE, FOUND 30 JULY 2026: the headstone at the Holon Cemetery, Bat Yam, reads
2 CONT "MALKA MOSKAL nee SCHAFIR", and names her FATHER: "MENDEL". Her married surname, her
2 CONT MAIDEN NAME and her patronymic are all three carved on the one stone - so the stone by
2 CONT itself proves she was a daughter of Menachem Mendel Schafir who married a Moskal.
2 CONT This is the FIRST DOCUMENT to give her date of death: 8 June 2003 / 8 Sivan 5763.
2 CONT David's burial place is known to the family; no search for it is needed (Amotz, 3 Aug 2026).
