1 NOTE _CONF PROVEN. Marriage act 18/1903 Wojslawice (APL fond 35/1787; scan in family folder)
2 CONT names him JUDKA-LEJBA MOSKAL, 20 (NOT 25 - corrected 21 Aug 2026 from the scan itself),
2 CONT bachelor, born in and living in the village of Krasniczyn, GMINA CZAJKI, son of DUVID
2 CONT and INDA nee RAJS. Married 29 Jul OS / 11 Aug 1903 NS at six in the evening; witnesses
2 CONT the szkolnicy Abram Guz, 45, and Gerszon Gonik, 41; bride Cywia-Dwojra Alspektor, 18.
2 CONT DOCUMENTARY CHAIN: birth act 15/1884 -> birth certificate -> marriage act 18/1903, the
2 CONT last citing the first explicitly.
2 CONT Earlier NAME CONFLICT: Malka wrote "Leib" on the 1957 forms and "Shmuel" on the
2 CONT 2001 forms. Most likely a double name SHMUEL-LEIB, of which each filing preserved one half.
2 CONT The business directories settle everyday usage: he traded as "Moskal L." - Polish L-slash
2 CONT being the standard abbreviation for Lejb. The family remembers him as Lejb.
2 CONT THE SHOP: listed in four consecutive annual directories -
2 CONT 1926/27 and 1928 under Galanterja (haberdashery/notions); 1929 under Piwiarnie (beer retail,
2 CONT as "Moskal D." - either Dvora or David); 1930 under Wody gazowe (soda water).
2 CONT This corroborates the family memory of a kiosk selling food and ice cream.
