2 NOTE ** Birth act 3/1881, Wojslawice - the son "Josef" already known from the birth index as a
3 CONT child of Szmul and Pesia-Ruchla. ** His Page of Testimony 1125024 gives age 60 in 1942
3 CONT (=> b. ~1882), one year off the act - a normal margin. (His second Page, 483774, says
3 CONT b. 1890; that year is rejected, see the identity note below.)
1 OCCU Roof-tiler and roofer - his father's trade
1 RESI
2 PLAC Wojslawice, Chelm, Lublin, Poland
2 NOTE Houses 32-33 on the survivors' map are marked SZAFIR - an adjoining pair, consistent with
3 CONT two Szafir households.
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1942
2 PLAC Wojslawice, Chelm, Lublin, Poland
2 CAUS Murdered in the Shoah
1 NOTE _CONF PROVEN as a separate Wojslawice Szafir household, in the necrology: "Shafir Yosef
2 CONT and his wife Yokheved". PROBABLE that this household is closely related to Mendel Schafir's:
2 CONT both families' professions include ROOFER and TILER (as did Mendel's father Shmuel), and
2 CONT both have Volhynian origins - Mendel's wife Perl was born at Wlodzimierz Wolynski and this
2 CONT family's daughter Dvora at Uscilug, twenty kilometres away.
2 CONT A "YOSELE SCHAFER THE ROOF-TILER" was shot off a farmer's roof by Germans for sport in 1942
2 CONT ("he fell with his arms spread like a bird, and the Germans laughed out loud"). A Yosele
2 CONT Schafer was also a DOZOR - a member of the kehilla board. The family knows the roof story.
2 CONT ** OPEN QUESTION ANSWERED, 14 Aug 2026 - AND THE EARLIER RULING REVERSED. ** Until now
2 CONT this household was held to be a different Szafir family, and the note on Mendel's son
2 CONT Yosef says so explicitly ("the contradiction was checked and decided"). That ruling was
2 CONT made before the Pages of Testimony were read. Two of them name this man's parents
2 CONT outright: 1125024 "father Shmuel, mother Pesia" and 483774 "father Shmuel, mother Peshe".
2 CONT Szmul Szaufer (@I1001@) married PESIA-Ruchla Szyfman in 1873, was himself a ROOFER, and had
2 CONT a son JOSEF registered at birth act 3/1881. Father's name, mother's rare given name,
2 CONT the trade, the town and the birth year all converge on one man.
2 CONT ⇒ He is Mendel's own brother, and the "second Szafir household" of houses 32-33 is the
2 CONT family he founded, next door to his parents'. The roof story is about Amotz's
2 CONT great-grandfather's brother.
2 CONT ⚠ WHAT THIS DOES NOT SETTLE: the note at Mendel's son Yosef (the other Yosef Schafir,
2 CONT Malka's brother) still carries the old ruling and should be revised to match.
