3 CONT Wojslawice (APL 35/1787/0/2.1/39, unit 2196593, scan 37) marries his son JANKIEL and
3 CONT calls him "syn POKOJNYKH Lejby i Brandli urozhdennoj Ejlovoj zakonnykh suprugov
3 CONT Moskalyuv" - THE LATE Lejba AND Brandla. Corroborated independently by marriage act
3 CONT 1/1878 (Dawid-Szloma), "synom POKOJNYKH Lejby i Brandli urozhdennoj EJL".
3 CONT >>> DISPROVES the Robinson tree's "Lejba Moskal d. 1892" by ~17 years. He is also
3 CONT absent from the Wojslawice death indexes of 1891 and 1892 (read 17 Aug 2026).
3 CONT >>> SEARCH WINDOW for his death act: 1866-1874 (1848-1864 swept clean for all names;
3 CONT the 1865 volume does not exist in the fond). Indexes 1870, 1871 and 1872 were read
3 CONT line by line on 20 Aug 2026 - NO MOSKAL in any of them. Remaining: 1866, 1867, 1868,
3 CONT 1869 (volumes on disk), 1873, 1874. CAVEAT: Krasniczyn Jews also registered at
3 CONT UCHANIE (fond 1781), so a Wojslawice negative is not absolute.
1 NOTE _CONF PROVEN ancestor since 4 Aug 2026: marriage act 1/1878 Wojslawice names Dawid-Szloma
2 CONT Moskal as son of THE LATE LEJBA AND BRANDLYA NEE EIL, Moskal spouses - the very household
2 CONT below. Earlier assessment (kept for the record): A documented Moskal farming household in the villages
2 CONT immediately around Wojslawice, 1842-1889, headed by Lejba Moskal (b. c.1817) and his wife
2 CONT Braina/Brandla. Children recorded: Kielman 1842, Hana 1844 (of Teratyn), Abram Moszko 1848,
2 CONT Jankiel 1851, Dawid Szloma 1854, Henia (m. an Erlich 1867), plus marriages of Abram Moszko
2 CONT 1866 (of Krasniczyn, Wojslawice district), Abram Hersz 1876 and Aron Moszko 1881.
2 CONT TWO REASONS TO PURSUE: (1) the given name - David's father was Lejb, and Ashkenazi families
2 CONT named children after dead grandparents, so a Lejb born in the 1870s is what a Lejba of 1817
2 CONT produces two generations down. (2) DISPROVED, kept for the record: I suspected the
2 CONT mother's maiden name "Eil"/"Ajl" was a clerk's abbreviation of AJLSPEKTOR/ALSPEKTOR,
2 CONT which would have put a Moskal-Alspektor marriage in the 1840s. It is not. Marriage act
2 CONT 1/1882 Wojslawice shows AJL as a standalone Wojslawice surname with its own household -
2 CONT Moszek Ajl married to Malka nee Kriger. Brandla was an Ajl, full stop.
2 CONT >>> TO RESOLVE: register images. Source: JRI-Poland index records.
