1 NOTE >>> HIS PARENTS ARE NOT ENTERED, DELIBERATELY. Uchanie marriage act 1/1839 calls him
2 CONT "Lejbus LEYBOWICZ, son of Herszek Leybowicz and CHAJA" of Krasniczyn - patronymics,
2 CONT no surname. Wojslawice death act 29/1847 names a MOSZKO MOSKAL @I1146@, aged 27, of
2 CONT the same village and the same trade, "son of HERSZEK and SURA, SPOUSES MOSKAL, OF
2 CONT KRASNICZYN". That act is the first document ever to write MOSKAL on that generation,
2 CONT and it makes Lejba and Moszko very probably brothers.
2 CONT ** But the bridge "Lejbus Leybowicz = Lejba Moskal" is still INFERENCE, and the
2 CONT mother's name differs between the two acts (Chaja in 1839, Sura in 1847). Until one
2 CONT of those is settled, Herszek @I1150@ and Sura @I1151@ are attached to Moszko ONLY. **
2 CONT >>> WHAT WOULD SETTLE IT: the 1839 allegata - AP Lublin, signature 35/1781/0/2/49,
2 CONT "Alegaty do ksiag urodzen, malzenstw i zgonow z lat 1839-1843". It should contain
2 CONT Lejbus's birth extract, naming his parents and his family name.
2 CONT ** NOT DIGITISED, and it cannot be pulled online. ** Requested from AP Lublin;
2 CONT answered 21 Aug 2026 by Anna Chursan, ref. UZA.6342.2292.2026.ACH: "the allegata
2 CONT are not digitised. We can make copies FOR A FEE, if the annexes to act 1/1839
2 CONT survived. Note that not every couple submitted documents - an oral declaration
2 CONT usually sufficed. Information on this will be sent to you later."
2 CONT ⇒ THE REQUEST IS LIVE; the archive is checking whether the annexes survive.
2 CONT >>> CITE THE SIGNATURE, NOT AN ID. The archive replied that it does not use the
2 CONT portal "identyfikator" and could not tell what 1790469 referred to. Checked
2 CONT 21 Aug 2026: unit 1790469 is in fact sygn. 2/48, the 1834-1838 allegata - a
2 CONT DIFFERENT unit, and it too has no scans.

