1 NOTE >>> IDENTIFIED IN FULL, 6 Aug 2026 - DEATH ACT 4/1869.
2 CONT Found via the 1869 alphabetical death index (unit 2196573, scan 38, entry 12:
2 CONT "SZYFMAN Moszko Gersz, act 4"). The act itself is unit 2196573, scan 32, LEFT page, p.52.
2 CONT "Drawn up in the town of Wojslawice on 21 FEBRUARY 1869 at eleven in the morning.
2 CONT Appeared the Jewish residents of Wojslawice JOS RAJS, master, forty-three years of age,
2 CONT and JANKIEL KANTOR, szkolnik (synagogue beadle), fifty-seven, and declared that
2 CONT ON 19 FEBRUARY of this year at one after midnight died, resident in the town of
2 CONT Wojslawice, the Jewish LABOURER (rabotnik) MOSZKO GERSZ SZYFMAN /Moszko Herz Szyfman/,
2 CONT FORTY-SEVEN YEARS OF AGE, BORN IN THE VILLAGE OF SWIERZE, of the late JOS and DWOJRA
2 CONT nee BUKSZTAN, lawful spouses SZYFMAN, LEAVING AFTER HIM THE WIDOWED WIFE DOJRA SZYFMAN
2 CONT NEE KAC."
2 CONT >>> THE WIDOW IS OUR DWOJRA-ITTA @I1052@. She is "Dwojra Szyfman nee Kac", she is a widow
2 CONT from Feb 1869, and in her own death act five years later (6/1874) she is exactly that:
2 CONT a widow, aged 55, living with her relatives. The fit is complete.
2 CONT >>> THE THREE NAMES ARE ONE MAN. Three clerks, three renderings of a multi-part Yiddish
2 CONT name: "MOSZKO GERSZ" (1869, his own death act, the best of the three), "GERSZKO"
2 CONT (1872, daughter Estera-Dwojra's death act), "BEREK" (1873, daughter Pesia-Ruchla's
2 CONT marriage act). All three attach the same wife, Dwojra-Itta nee Kac. Primary name in this
2 CONT file is now MOSZKO-GERSZ, on the strength of the act that is about him.
2 CONT #proof PROVEN.
1 NOTE >>> ★ OPEN QUESTION OF THE FIRST ORDER, raised 6 Aug 2026 by the DOROHUSK index.
2 CONT "1836, marriage act 2 - SZYFMAN HERSZEK, male, NINETEEN, village of Dorohusk, son of
2 CONT JOSIA and DWORA" married "KAC DWOIRA LAIA, female, SEVENTEEN, daughter of MOSZEK
2 CONT and PESA".
2 CONT FOR: Herszek = Gersz. Son of Jos and Dwojra - the same parents. The bride is a
2 CONT DWOJRA KAC. Her age gives b. ~1819 - EXACTLY our Dwojra-Itta's year (55 in 1874).
2 CONT And an 1836 marriage would explain why no marriage act exists in Wojslawice 1841-56,
2 CONT and why children only appear from ~1850 (earlier ones simply not yet found).
2 CONT ★ And their daughter was called PESIA-Ruchla - Pesa is this bride's mother.
2 CONT AGAINST, AND IT IS SERIOUS: her parents here are MOSZEK and PESA, but Dwojra-Itta's
2 CONT own death act 6/1874 - declared by her son-in-law Szmul Szaufer - says SZMUL and
2 CONT ESTERA KAC. That is a flat contradiction, not a spelling variant.
2 CONT AND: Herszek b. ~1817 vs our man's ~1822 (from one 1869 act). Five years.
2 CONT AND: KAC is one of the commonest names in this district - the rule established the
2 CONT same day is that a Kac hit is weak until the act itself is read.
2 CONT >>> ✖ REJECTED THE SAME DAY. The act itself was read (APL 35/1774/0/1/33, scan 29,
2 CONT LEFT page; the fond is zespol id 4203, unit 2194403, "Ksiega malzenstw" 1829-1867).
2 CONT "2. Drawn up in the village of [Swierze/Sniatycze] on 24 MAY 1836 at three in the
2 CONT afternoon. Appeared the Jew Moszko [Aber], rabbi of the parish, together with the Jew
2 CONT HERSZEK SZYFMAN, RESIDENT IN THE VILLAGE OF DOROHUSK, NINETEEN, BORN IN THE VILLAGE
2 CONT OF DOROHUSK, of JOS SZYFMAN and DWORA SZYFMANOWA, spouses, DAY-LABOURERS RESIDENT IN
2 CONT THE VILLAGE OF DOROHUSK - and with DWOJRA LAJA KAC, SPINSTER, SEVENTEEN, [daughter]
2 CONT of MOSZKO KAC, day-labourer, and PESA KAC, spouses, living here... in the presence of
2 CONT JOS SZYFMAN, father of the groom, [and] HERSZKO KAC, grandfather."
2 CONT ⇒ THE BRIDE IS A LOCAL DOROHUSK GIRL, daughter of Moszko and Pesa Kac, with a
2 CONT grandfather Herszko Kac present. OUR Dwojra-Itta was BORN IN THE POSAD OF WOJSLAWICE
2 CONT and her parents were SZMUL and ESTERA KAC. Different woman, different family.
2 CONT ⇒ HERSZEK IS A THIRD BROTHER, not our Moszko-Gersz. Hypothesis closed. Do not reopen.
2 CONT ★ WHAT THE READING DID GIVE: JOS SZYFMAN WAS ALIVE IN MAY 1836, living in DOROHUSK
2 CONT and working as a ZAROBNIK (day-labourer) - the first statement of his occupation and
2 CONT the latest date at which he is known to be alive. Recorded at @I1083@.
2 CONT ◐ The act names both parents as "spouses resident in Dorohusk" without saying whether
2 CONT the mother was living; only the father is listed as present. That is consistent with
2 CONT Dwojra's death in 1833 but does not confirm it.
