3 CONT APL 35/1774/0/1/5 = unit 2194412, SCAN 12, LEFT page, p.30. ⚠ The volume is catalogued
3 CONT "1829-1863" but is a FRAGMENT out of chronological order: scan 4 = 1830, scans 6-9 =
3 CONT 1835, scan 10 = the 1835 index, and 1833 sits at scans 11-12 under a heading "Rok 1833".
3 CONT "No. 6ty. Drawn up in SWIERZE on the [thir]teenth of OCTOBER 1833 ... died DWORA
3 CONT SZYFMAN, a woman RESIDENT IN THE VILLAGE OF DOROHUSK, FORTY-FIVE YEARS OF AGE,
3 CONT DAUGHTER OF ARON AND PERLA, SPOUSES BUKSZPAN, OF DOROHUSK, leaving after her a
3 CONT WIDOWED HUSBAND, JOS SZYFMAN."
3 CONT ◐ the day of the month is the one word I would not swear to; the year, age, parents,
3 CONT residence and surviving husband are all unambiguous.
3 CONT Corroborated by Dorohusk marriage act 1/1832 ("Josia and Dwojra BUKSZPAN").
3 CONT ⚠ CLARIFIED 28 Aug 2026: act 1/1832 is NOT her own marriage - it is the marriage
3 CONT of her SON MOSZEK (aged 20) to Rane Katz, in which she and Jos appear as the
3 CONT GROOM'S PARENTS. Good corroboration of the couple; not a record of her marriage.
3 CONT >>> HER OWN MARRIAGE therefore falls c.1810-1812, INSIDE the mixed-register period
3 CONT when the Catholic parish priest registered Jews - and it would name ARON and PERLA.
3 CONT TARGET: fond 35/1932 (Swierze, filia Dorohusk) or 35/1931 (Swierze), marriages
3 CONT 1810-1812, both fully digitised. NOT YET SEARCHED.
3 CONT ⇒ SHE DIED AT DOROHUSK, not Swierze - the family had moved the few km down the Bug.
3 CONT ⇒ AND JOS OUTLIVED HER, which the 1836 marriage act independently confirms.
