2 CONT "Buksztanowoj". Read at full 3500px resolution; the initial letter is unambiguously B.
2 CONT >>> ↩ REVISED 6 Aug 2026, AFTER THE SWIERZE SWEEP. The Swierze register (815 records,
2 CONT JRI-indexed) contains NO Buksztan. It does contain BUKSZPAN (Chaim Bukszpan, d. 1835
2 CONT aged 46) and BUKSMAN (17 records). In Cyrillic "Букшпан" and "Букштан" differ by one
2 CONT letter. Since BUKSZPAN is an attested family in the very village where her son was
2 CONT born, BUKSZPAN looked the likelier reading.
2 CONT >>> ●● SETTLED THE SAME DAY. The DOROHUSK index states it outright, twice and
2 CONT independently of the Wojslawice act: marriage 1/1832 "Josia and Dwojra BUKSZPAN",
2 CONT and death 6/1833 "SZYFMAN / BUKSZPAN Dwera ... nee BUKSZPAN". THE SURNAME IS
2 CONT BUKSZPAN. "Buksztan" was my misreading of the Cyrillic and is kept only as an
2 CONT alternate name so the error stays visible.
2 CONT >>> Her granddaughter Pesia-Ruchla's elder sister was named ESTERA-DWOJRA and her own
2 CONT daughter-in-law was DWOJRA-ITTA - the name Dwojra runs hard through this family.
