2 CONT of Gierszon Rays", where he signed. FOUND 12 Aug 2026 - a wholly new generation.
2 CONT >>> ALIVE 1851: the inspection protocol at the end of the 1851 volume (APL
3 CONT 35/1787/0/2.1/16, scan 29 right) faults birth act 2 of 1851 because after the words
3 CONT "Wolfa Rajs Rzeznika" the clerk left out the words giving his age. So he was in
3 CONT Wojslawice in 1851, declaring a birth - and the one figure we want was the one omitted.
2 CONT >>> HIS DEATH ACT HAS NOT BEEN FOUND. Every surviving Wojslawice death index from 1848
3 CONT to 1884 has now been read (see findings/HUNT-wolf-rajs-death-act.md); the only Rajs
3 CONT deaths in 37 years are Paja 1855, Lea 1868, Dwojra 1871, Szulim 1872 and Anszel 1883.
3 CONT So he died either after 1884 (the register runs to 1913, unswept) or outside the town.
2 CONT ⚠ A "Wulf Rajs, 63" declares a death on 31 Dec 1878 (act 17/1878). Age 63 -> b. ~1815,
3 CONT which cannot be the father of a man born 1829. Either a second Wolf Rajs in the town,
3 CONT or a bad age. NOT resolved - and NOT assumed to be this man.
1 SOUR @S1023@
1 FAMS @F1040@

