1 NOTE Bukszpan of DOROHUSK, Chelm district - the act says "z Dorohuska", so the family
2 CONT itself was of Dorohusk. Established by death act 6/1833 of their daughter Dwojra,
2 CONT read in the original.
2 CONT >>> "BUKSZPAN Chaim, d. 1835 act 4, aged 46, son of SRUL and HYNDA, wife Ester Hynda
2 CONT Fiszlowicz". Born ~1789, one year after Dwojra, same village - but his parents are
2 CONT SRUL AND HYNDA, so he is NOT her brother. A second Bukszpan household. Do not confuse.
2 CONT >>> SEARCHED FOR THEM, 7 Aug 2026, AND NOT FOUND:
2 CONT (a) JRI, Surname=Bukszpan exact, Lublin gubernia: 149 records. EXACTLY ONE names Aron
2 CONT and Perla - Dwojra's own death act. No siblings of hers are indexed anywhere.
2 CONT (b) Given-name searches for Aron / Perla among Swierze and Dorohusk deaths: 5 hits,
2 CONT none of them Bukszpan.
2 CONT (c) The death indexes of every surviving ANNUAL volume were read: 1834 (3 deaths),
2 CONT 1835 (8), 1836 (10), 1843 (10), 1844 (3), 1845 (3), 1846 (11), 1847 (4) - 52 deaths,
2 CONT no Aron, no Perla, no Szyfman.
2 CONT ⇒ THEY MOST LIKELY DIED IN A GAP: the fond holds NO VOLUME for 1837-1842 and none for
2 CONT 1820-1825. Or they died before 1826, when Jewish civil registration in Congress Poland
2 CONT began at all - in which case no act ever existed.
2 CONT ⚠ AND A STRUCTURAL CEILING WORTH STATING: surnames were imposed on Congress Poland's
2 CONT Jews only c.1821. Before that Aron was not "Bukszpan" but "Aron son of ---", so even a
2 CONT surviving pre-1821 document could not be found by searching the surname.
1 SOUR @S1014@

