1 NOTE ADDED 21 Aug 2026 as the mother of MOSZKO @I1146@ ONLY.
2 CONT ** UNRESOLVED CONTRADICTION. ** Uchanie marriage act 1/1839 names the mother of
2 CONT Lejbus Leybowicz as CHAJA, who was present and gave her consent. Death act 29/1847
2 CONT names Moszko's mother as SURA. Three readings, none decided:
2 CONT (1) a double name, Chaja-Sura or Sura-Chaja - the simplest;
2 CONT (2) two marriages of Herszek, which would make Lejba and Moszko HALF-brothers;
2 CONT (3) two different Herszeks in Krasniczyn - least likely: same village, same trade,
2 CONT same decade.
2 CONT >>> THE TEST would be a death act for Chaja or for Sura. NEITHER is in the
2 CONT Wojslawice death indexes for 1841-1848 or 1848-1884.
2 CONT >>> CANDIDATE ELIMINATED 21 Aug 2026: "Muskal Fryjna, death 16/1849" DOES NOT EXIST.
2 CONT The 1849 alphabetical death index was read off the film (sygn. 2.1/14, scan 30):
2 CONT nineteen deaths, listed in full, and the ONLY Muskal in it is row 12, SZYFRA,
2 CONT act 16, page 79 - Moszko's little daughter @I1149@, already read and entered.
2 CONT "Fryjna" was a misreading of "Szyfra" in the same act.
2 CONT >>> SECOND CANDIDATE ELIMINATED 21 Aug 2026: "Moskal Perla, death 16/1873" was
2 CONT read in the original. She is PERLA nee PERZ @I1152@, born ~1844 in Tyszowce and
2 CONT dead at TWENTY-NINE - a full generation too young to be Herszek's wife.
2 CONT ** BOTH proposed local tests are now closed. ** Neither Chaja nor Sura died in
2 CONT the Wojslawice district, and no further candidate exists in its indexes.
2 CONT >>> THE QUESTION NOW HAS NO LOCAL TEST. It moves to Krasniczyn (fond 1747,
2 CONT from 1826) and to the 1839 Uchanie allegata, which is with AP Lublin.
2 CONT >>> DO NOT CONFUSE WITH SURA nee ERLICH @I1147@, Moszko's wife.
1 SOUR @S1043@
