1 FAMS @F1073@
1 NOTE FIRST WIFE OF ARON CUKIER @I71@ - new to the file, 28 Aug 2026.
2 CONT >>> SHE MAY BE THE MOTHER OF ABRAM ~1821 (@I78@) AND MORTKA ~1823 (@I81@), who on
2 CONT the present reckoning were born before Aron married Tauba in January 1824. Their
2 CONT own marriage acts of 1844 name their mother as Tauba Moskowicz, which is what one
2 CONT would expect of a stepmother who raised them from infancy - but it is equally
2 CONT possible the ages stated in 1844 are simply two or three years out. UNRESOLVED, and
2 CONT deliberately left so: the children remain attached to @F64@ and are NOT moved.
2 CONT >>> The witness SZLAMA RUTKOSKI, 45, potasznik of Ruda, who signed the 1824 act in
2 CONT Hebrew letters, is almost certainly her father or brother.
2 CONT >>> ** AN UNRESOLVED CONTRADICTION IN HER DEATH ACT, LEFT VISIBLE ON PURPOSE. **
2 CONT The first declarant is "Starozakonny MORTKA CUKROWICZ maiacy lat siedmdziesiat,
2 CONT OYCIEC ZMARLEY" - Mortka Cukrowicz, seventy, FATHER OF THE DECEASED. The wording is
2 CONT unambiguous in the manuscript. But that same Mortka is Aron's own father, named as
2 CONT such by the Checiny kahal certificate and by the marriage act; if he were also
2 CONT Sara's father, Aron would have married his sister, which is impossible.
2 CONT The reading that survives is that the clerk wrote "oyciec" where he meant
2 CONT father-in-law. The alternative - two men called Mortka Cukrowicz, both potaszniks
2 CONT at Ruda, both about seventy in 1823 - is weakened by the ages matching across the
2 CONT two acts (70 in September, 71 in October).
2 CONT >>> THE ORIGINAL ACT 16/1823 must be read before this is called settled.
2 CONT The second declarant is ABRAM RUDNICKI, 24, also a potasznik at Ruda - a name new
2 CONT to the file and not entered.
2 CONT _BRANCH albert
1 SOUR @S1049@
1 SOUR @S1051@

