1 NOTE (documented, by name) BROTHER OF ARON @I71@ - new to the file, 28 August 2026. He is
2 CONT the first declarant of his father's death in Checiny in 1823: "stawili sie
2 CONT Starozakonni JOACHYM CUKROWSKI Syn zmarlego, Handlarz [...] w Miescie Checinach
2 CONT zamieszkali". No age is given for him and nothing else about him is yet known.
2 CONT >>> He stayed in Checiny while Aron moved out to Ruda Strawczynska. Checiny records
2 CONT of the 1820s-40s should carry his marriage and children.
2 CONT >>> THE PLACE TO LOOK IS NOW KNOWN: the separate JEWISH civil register of Checiny
2 CONT (akta stanu cywilnego wyznania mojzeszowego) survives and is scanned in full from
2 CONT 1826 to 1942 - GenBaza album "Checiny_moj_AP Kielce", one volume per year. It begins
2 CONT in 1826 because that is when separate Jewish registers began; nothing of this family
2 CONT before 1826 can be in it.
2 CONT _BRANCH albert
1 NOTE (documented) HIS MARRIAGE - act 23 of the Checiny register for 1823, karta 211, read
2 CONT from the image 29 August 2026 (@S1055@): on 19 July 1823 he married GITLA FRAYMOWA,
2 CONT 34, daughter of Jowie Wolfowicz and Pinda z Wolfow. See @F1077@.
2 CONT >>> ** THE MARRIAGE ACT GIVES HIS FATHER A DIFFERENT PATRONYMIC. ** It calls him
2 CONT "Syn MARTKA SZMULOWICZA w Rudzie Strawczynskiey i Gminie zamieszkalego" - son of
2 CONT Mortka SON OF SZMUL - and his mother "Estery z L[...]ow, a teraz zwana Cukrowska".
2 CONT But the death act of that same father, drawn by the SAME registrar three months
2 CONT later, reads "Rodzicow WULFA i DWOYRY Cukrowskich [...] Syn", and the Checiny kahal
2 CONT certificate of December 1823 calls the couple "WULFOWICZOW na teraz Cukrowskich".
2 CONT Both words were checked at maximum magnification and both are unambiguous in the
2 CONT manuscript: this is a conflict between the documents, not a misreading.
2 CONT TWO DOCUMENTS SAY WULF, ONE SAYS SZMUL. Wulf and Dwojra therefore stand in the tree,
2 CONT and the Szmulowicz form is recorded rather than acted on. One possibility worth
2 CONT testing: that Wulf was himself WULF SZMULOWICZ, and the July clerk reached a
2 CONT generation too far back.
2 CONT >>> The mother's family is given differently too - "z L[...]ow" here against
2 CONT "z Choynow" / "z Chaynow" in the 1824 marriage act and in the kahal certificate.
1 SOUR @S1052@
1 SOUR @S1056@
1 SOUR @S1055@

