1 TITL Chęciny civil register 1823, death act 220 - the ORIGINAL act of Mortka Cukrowski
1 AUTH Rev. Antoni Jedryszko, Mansionarius, deputy Registrar of Civil Status of gmina Checiny
1 PUBL Archiwum Panstwowe w Kielcach, Checiny civil register for 1823 (60 karty). Karta 318, act 220. GenBaza album "Checiny_AP Kielce / 1823", scan _22_087.jpg (image 88 of 99); the alphabetical death index is on scans 95-97.
1 NOTE READ FROM THE IMAGE, 29 August 2026. This is the ORIGINAL act, not the certified
2 CONT extract @S1052@ that was filed with the 1824 marriage. It confirms the extract word
2 CONT for word AND settles the date: "Dnia TRZYDZIESTEGO PAZDZIERNIKA" - the thirtieth of
3 CONT OCTOBER 1823, the death "na Dniu wczorayszym o godzinie siodmey wieczor" - the day
3 CONT before, at seven in the evening. The month caveat recorded on 28 August is closed.
2 CONT >>> The act adds a line the extract does not stress: "Po czem Oswiadczaiacy PODPISALI
2 CONT PO HEBRAYSZKU z Nami niniejszy Akt Zeyscia" - the declarants signed in HEBREW, and
3 CONT two Hebrew signatures stand on the page. The first reads CHAIM CUKROWSKI, which is
3 CONT the Hebrew name of the man the Polish clerk calls JOACHYM (@I1184@). The second is
3 CONT the witness Herszla Waxman; its reading is less certain.
2 CONT Located through the volume's own alphabetical death index: entry 30, "Cukrowski
2 CONT Mortka, lat 71, karta 318".
2 CONT Local copy: albert/sources/checiny-1823/p88.jpg (index: p94-p97).

0 @S1055@ SOUR
1 TITL Chęciny civil register 1823, marriage act 23 - Jochym Cukrowski and Gitla Fraymowa, 19 July 1823
1 AUTH Rev. Antoni Jedryszko, Mansionarius, deputy Registrar of Civil Status of gmina Checiny
1 PUBL Archiwum Panstwowe w Kielcach, Checiny civil register for 1823. Karta 211, act 23. GenBaza album "Checiny_AP Kielce / 1823", scan _22_051.jpg (image 52 of 99); the alphabetical marriage index is on scan 60, entry 19: "Jachym Cukrowski i Gitla Fraymowa - 211".
1 NOTE READ FROM THE IMAGE, 29 August 2026. Found first in the Swietogen index (indexer:
2 CONT Edward Jablonski), then read in the register itself.
2 CONT >>> Swietogen indexes the CATHOLIC parish of Checiny (births 1766-1917, marriages
2 CONT 1766-1919, deaths 1789-1905). There is NO "Checiny Mojzeszowi" entry in its parish
3 CONT list, so the separate JEWISH register from 1826 on is NOT indexed there. The two
3 CONT Cukrowski records it does hold - this marriage and death act 220 - are both of 1823,
3 CONT before the registers split, which is why they fall inside its coverage at all.
2 CONT A Hebrew signature line stands under the act. It is NOT confidently legible at this
2 CONT resolution and no reading of it is recorded here.
2 CONT Local copy: albert/sources/checiny-1823/p52.jpg (index: p60.jpg).

