1 NAME Dawid Jakob /Rywenbajrych/
2 GIVN Dawid Jakob
2 SURN Rywenbajrych
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 JUL 1858
2 PLAC Klimontow, Radom Gubernia, Poland
2 NOTE Born 18/30 July 1858 at one in the afternoon, in the town of Klimontow. Registered
3 CONT 31 July / 12 August 1858 at five in the morning.
3 CONT DECLARANT: his father HERCYK RYWENBAJRYCH, trader, aged 43 - his own age statement,
3 CONT which gives a birth year of about 1815. Witnesses: Moszek Agater, 43, and Ejzyk Kimet,
3 CONT 44, both szkolnicy (synagogue beadles) of Klimontow. Mother: RUCHLA, aged 36, giving
3 CONT about 1822 - and the act does NOT give her maiden name, which is why it stands as the
3 CONT one blank in the series of readings recorded at @I8@.
3 CONT >>> HIS FATHER SIGNED THE ACT HIMSELF, in Hebrew letters, beneath the Polish text.
3 CONT Registrar: Ludwik Gnoinski.
1 FAMC @F4@
1 NOTE (documented) Klimontow BIRTH ACT 25/1858, READ FROM THE IMAGE 29 Aug 2026. He was
2 CONT named in the note on @F4@ from the start but had never been given a record of his own;
2 CONT entered now, from the act rather than from that note.
2 CONT No death act has been located for him. He is not among the children whose deaths the
2 CONT register records (Fajga Perla 1857, Dawid Hersz 1862, Szymcha 1864, Chaskiel 1865,
2 CONT Necha 1869), so on present evidence he outlived infancy - but nothing traces him
2 CONT further, and the household lost both parents in 1867, when he was nine.
2 CONT >>> THE NAME-REUSE QUESTION IS NOW ANSWERED, AND THE ANSWER IS NO. A younger brother
2 CONT was named DAWID HERSZL in 1861, and two living sons both called Dawid looked unusual
2 CONT enough to suggest that Dawid Jakob had died and his name been reused. The Klimontow
2 CONT death registers were read for the whole window on 29 Aug 2026, from the images:
2 CONT   1858 - annual index, 33 deaths - no Rywenbajrych
2 CONT   1859 - annual index, 38 deaths - no Rywenbajrych
2 CONT   1860 - acts 1-12 (Jan to 10 May) read one by one - no Rywenbajrych
2 CONT   1861 - annual index, 58 deaths - no Rywenbajrych
2 CONT ⚠ ONE GAP REMAINS, and it is a gap in the filming, not in my reading: volume
3 CONT 1852-1860_zg ends at act 12 of 1860 and volume 1861-1870_zg opens at act 23, so
3 CONT ACTS 13-22 OF 1860 - roughly mid-May to mid-August - are in neither filmed volume.
2 CONT ⇒ On the evidence, HE DID NOT DIE AS AN INFANT. The two Dawids were two living
2 CONT brothers, distinguished by their second names, Jakob and Herszl.
2 CONT _BRANCH albert
1 SOUR @S1057@

